  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 100 PM EST Friday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry, and breezy tonight and tomorrow. A cold \nfront brings another round of rain Sunday night into Monday. \n\nStrong sfc low pressure over the eastern Great Lakes continues\nto move northeast supporting a gusty southwest wind this \nafternoon. Conditions will remain mixed this evening and tonight\nwith a persistent breeze from the southwest and west. Winds \ngusting to 25 to 30+ mph this afternoon will decrease to 10 to \n20 mph overnight. Cooler tonight with lows generally in the \nupper 30s to around 40 near the coast. \n\nSaturday will not be as windy as high pressure builds in from\nthe west though with mixing westerly winds will still gust to 12\nto 25 mph with the highest wind near the Bay and coast and over\nNE NC. Expect more sun Saturday with highs in the upper 50s to\nnear 60. Clearer skies and calming conditions will allow lows to\ndrop into the mid 30s by Sunday morning with some low 30s\npossible. \n\nFor Sunday clouds gradually increase from the west and winds \nwill be lighter. Temps become even milder with highs mid 60s \nSunday. A cold front approaches the area late Sunday and \npasses through quickly sometime Monday morning. While it does \nlook like this will bring additional rain to the area Sunday \nnight, QPF does not last long. Model ensembles suggest \ngenerally a third of an inch or less of rainfall. Probs for a \nhalf an inch of rainfall are decreasing. A brief cool down with \nhigh back to the 50s is expected behind the front Monday through\nWednesday, but this likely won't last long given the weak upper\nlevel flow depicted in guidance.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Tides continue to decrease this evening, with \nlingering moderate/locally major flooding for the eastern shore,\nand minor flooding across the northern Neck and for sound-side \nflooding near the Albemarle and Currituck sound.\n\n\nWith elevated W to SW winds, along with ebb-tide dominance at \nthe mouth of the Bay, tidal anomalies have continued to \ndecrease across the region. Even with this trend, Coastal Flood\nWarnings remain in effect for much of the Maryland eastern shore\nand Accomack VA for moderate to locally Major flooding with the\ncurrent tide cycle. A Coastal Flood Advisory is in effect into\nearly evening for the northern Neck and also across VA Beach and\nportions of NE NC along the Albemarle and Currituck for sound- \nside flooding. However, this evening's high tide cycle should be\nthe last of the headlines, with nothing more than perhaps localized\nnuisance flooding across the bayside of the MD eastern shore \nSaturday morning.",
